From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ROG5 Linux Project <rog5-linux@localhost>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] phy: qcom: qmp-ufs: isolate symbol clock registration

Generation 37 localized target USB loss to qmp_ufs_register_clocks(), which
registers three fixed-rate symbol clocks before publishing the OF clock
provider. Advance the RAM-only SM8350 discriminator through only those three
passive clock-hardware registrations, then stop before OF provider publication
or cleanup-action registration.

The UFS core and host remain absent, so this diagnostic cannot enumerate or
access storage.

Signed-off-by: ROG5 Linux Project <rog5-linux@localhost>
---
 drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
@@ -2109,6 +2109,10 @@ static int qmp_ufs_register_clocks(struct qmp_ufs *qmp, struct device_node *np)
 
 	clk_data->hws[2] = hw;
 
+	if (of_device_is_compatible(qmp->dev->of_node,
+				    "qcom,sm8350-qmp-ufs-phy"))
+		return 0;
+
 	ret = of_clk_add_hw_provider(np, of_clk_hw_onecell_get, clk_data);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
@@ -2240,7 +2245,7 @@ static int qmp_ufs_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node,
 				    "qcom,sm8350-qmp-ufs-phy")) {
 		dev_notice(dev,
-			   "ROG5 QMP-UFS diagnostic: clock provider stage complete\n");
+			   "ROG5 QMP-UFS diagnostic: fixed-rate symbol clocks stage complete\n");
 		of_node_put(np);
 		return 0;
 	}
-- 
